Package: programmers-screenshot
Version: @VERSION@
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8),
         python3-gi,
         python3-gi-cairo,
         python3-cairo,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0,
         gir1.2-notify-0.7,
         xclip | wl-clipboard
Recommends: nautilus | dolphin | nemo | thunar,
            gnome-session-canberra | pulseaudio-utils | pipewire-bin | alsa-utils
Maintainer: Chris <chris@kademi.co>
Homepage: https://github.com/shubshub/programmers-screenshot
Description: Minimal region screenshot tool for hotkey binding
 Freezes the screen and puts a toolbar across the top. Mark out a region,
 draw on it with the pen, then press Capture. The result is copied to the
 clipboard and saved as a timestamped PNG in ~/Pictures/Screenshots,
 with a shutter sound and a notification offering to open the image or
 show it in its folder.
 .
 Tools are pluggable: a new one is a single file plus a registry line.
 .
 Includes region, freehand pen, line/circle/arrow and numbered step tools.
 .
 It does one thing on one keypress: no editor, no dialogs, no upload
 prompts. Register a GNOME shortcut with --install-hotkey, or point any
 shortcut at the programmers-screenshot command.
 .
 Works on GNOME under X11 and Wayland, and spans multi-monitor layouts.
